WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.848 --> 00:00:04.052
(operatic singing)

00:00:04.052 --> 00:00:06.576
- There's something
about standing on stage

00:00:06.576 --> 00:00:07.763
and thinking about the people

00:00:07.763 --> 00:00:10.282
that have doubted me in the past.

00:00:10.282 --> 00:00:11.907
Standing on stage and
thinking about the people

00:00:11.907 --> 00:00:14.193
who I would say, "Hello.",
to and they would just look

00:00:14.193 --> 00:00:17.180
at me and keep on walking.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:19.179
It's in that moment when I'm on stage

00:00:19.179 --> 00:00:21.041
when none of that mattered,

00:00:21.041 --> 00:00:25.041
where people see me as
more than just a janitor.

00:00:27.989 --> 00:00:29.330
I am Keanon Kyles.

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.174
I am an internationally
touring opera singer.

00:00:32.174 --> 00:00:35.142
I've performed at Lincoln
Center and Carnegie Hall

00:00:35.142 --> 00:00:38.629
and the Chicago Theatre, and
all these amazing venues,

00:00:38.629 --> 00:00:40.504
but at the end of the
day, in order to support

00:00:40.504 --> 00:00:45.117
those dreams and support
my life, I am a janitor.

00:00:45.117 --> 00:00:47.009
(wheels rolling)

00:00:47.009 --> 00:00:50.343
I am a janitor because bills are something

00:00:50.343 --> 00:00:52.626
that is very real (laughs),

00:00:52.626 --> 00:00:56.126
and as you get older, they get bigger.

00:00:56.126 --> 00:00:59.583
The assumptions that
people have about janitors,

00:00:59.583 --> 00:01:03.166
are that they are
uneducated, impoverished.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.837
I cannot tell you how
many looks I've gotten,

00:01:07.837 --> 00:01:09.924
and the side-eyes, because
they just think that,

00:01:09.924 --> 00:01:11.507
"Oh, you're just a janitor."

00:01:11.507 --> 00:01:13.772
It's so interesting
because they never took

00:01:13.772 --> 00:01:16.312
the time to really know who this person is

00:01:16.312 --> 00:01:18.895
that is cleaning up after them.

00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:22.341
Being an opera singer is very hard.

00:01:22.341 --> 00:01:25.604
It's not easy, technically,
because opera music

00:01:25.604 --> 00:01:26.937
is very complex.

00:01:29.565 --> 00:01:34.314
I meet with my vocal coach/mentor
once or twice a week,

00:01:34.314 --> 00:01:38.112
but I, myself, rehearse
probably two hours on top

00:01:38.112 --> 00:01:39.691
of that a day.

00:01:39.691 --> 00:01:44.034
I am currently rehearsing
this lead role of Rigoletto,

00:01:44.034 --> 00:01:46.125
for the Clyde Opera Group's production,

00:01:46.125 --> 00:01:47.125
in Scotland.

00:01:48.055 --> 00:01:50.972
(operatic singing)

00:01:54.059 --> 00:01:56.399
Rigoletto is my first title role,

00:01:56.399 --> 00:01:59.423
which makes this moment so amazing for me,

00:01:59.423 --> 00:02:03.590
because the whole opera is
about him and his story.

00:02:05.542 --> 00:02:08.943
Coming from being a janitor to starring

00:02:08.943 --> 00:02:11.360
in a show is very empowering.

00:02:12.274 --> 00:02:15.191
(operatic singing)

00:02:17.358 --> 00:02:22.286
Being a janitor has humbled me
and has grounded me so much.

00:02:22.286 --> 00:02:25.685
You have to hold onto
yourself because nobody

00:02:25.685 --> 00:02:27.968
cares about your dreams more than you do.

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:30.968
(operatic singing)

